This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Both of the rule's corpus and subject shapes apply, either alone being sufficient.

Its CORPUS is ledger.snapshot, a frozen copy of docs/backlog.md, this repository's own carry-over
backlog; a consumer tree gets no docs/backlog.md at all. Its SUBJECTS are scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh,
scripts/validate-backlog-size.sh and scripts/backlog-reverify.sh, none of which install.sh
copies: its copy loop derives from core/fixtures/ and core/scripts/ and never touches the
repo-root scripts/. On a consumer this fixture would resolve no validator and no ledger.

It holds the two real-ledger joins that used to be arm j1 of core/fixtures/backlog-receipt-binding/
and arm b16 of core/fixtures/backlog-size-ceiling/. BL-872 froze the ledger they read into
ledger.snapshot; against the live docs/backlog.md they run as arm R9 of
scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh at pre-push. Those two fixtures carry the same declaration for
the same reason.
